%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f0d9b320ba1bccb4f9fd7e7f2cb4c281, type: 3}
  m_Name: SIM-Card Scam
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScamCaseData
  caseId: C02
  queueNumber: A102
  caseTitle: Failed Delivery Scam
  scamType: Delivery Phishing Scam
  victimName: Emily Wong
  victimAge: 28
  victimOccupation: Office Administrator
  initialComplaint: HI... im Emily, I was approached by what I thought was a telecommunications
    company offering a limited-time chance to earn $100 by signing up for a SIM card.
    I gave them my NRIC details and a confirmation code, but I only realised later
    that a SIM card had been created under my name.
  lobbyNpcPrefab: {fileID: 1160195515370384998, guid: 282dbb64542aba2448f3bf95f599c3ec, type: 3}
  interviewNpcPrefab: {fileID: 1160195515370384998, guid: 282dbb64542aba2448f3bf95f599c3ec, type: 3}
  behaviourType: 2
  receptionDialogue: Hi, im Emily, I responded to an offer from what I thought was
    a telco company. I gave them my NRIC details and a confirmation code, and later
    I found out a SIM card had been created under my name.
  interviewDecisions:
  - npcLine: "Hi\u2026 I think someone used my details to register a SIM card. I
      only found out after everything had already happened."
    choices:
    - playerChoice: What did the company offer you?
      npcResponse: They said I could earn $100 if I signed up for a SIM card through
        them. They made it sound like a limited-time promotion, so I didn't want
        to miss the opportunity.
      unlockedFactIds:
      - fake_telco
      - one_hundred_dollar_offer
      - limited_time_offer
    - playerChoice: How did you even fall for the scam?
      npcResponse: 'The company offered me a "limited time" promotion of $100 and
        i didn''t want to lose the chance to earn. I really thought it was genuine. '
      unlockedFactIds:
      - limited_time_offer
  - npcLine: It started when I saw an offer from what looked like a telco company.
      They said I could get $100 if I signed up for a SIM card through them
    choices:
    - playerChoice: That sounds tempting. What did they ask you to do to sign up?
      npcResponse: "They asked for my NRIC details first. I thought that made sense
        because SIM cards need to be registered under someone\u2019s identity."
      unlockedFactIds:
      - nric_details
      - confirmation_code
    - playerChoice: You gave them your NRIC just for $100?
      npcResponse: "Yeah\u2026 I know it sounds bad now. At the time, the offer looked
        legitimate, and they made it sound like I had to act quickly."
      unlockedFactIds:
      - confirmation_code
  - npcLine: After that, I received a confirmation code on my phone, and they told
      me to send it to them so they could complete the registration.
    choices:
    - playerChoice: Did the message say what the confirmation code was actually authorising?
      npcResponse: "Not clearly. I thought it was just confirming that I was the
        person signing up. I didn\u2019t realise a simple code could actually approve
        the SIM registration."
      unlockedFactIds:
      - sim_card_created
      - nric_details
      - confirmation_code
    - playerChoice: You should never send confirmation codes to strangers.
      npcResponse: I know that now. But at the time, I thought I was dealing with
        a real telco representative.
      unlockedFactIds:
      - sim_card_created
  - npcLine: "I didn\u2019t realise anything was wrong until later, when I found
      out a SIM card had been registered under my name."
    choices:
    - playerChoice: How did you discover that the SIM card had been created?
      npcResponse: "I noticed something wasn\u2019t right and checked with the telco.
        That\u2019s when I found out there was another SIM registered using my details."
      unlockedFactIds:
      - sim_card_created
      - nric_details
      - confirmation_code
    - playerChoice: So you only checked after the damage was already done?
      npcResponse: "Yeah\u2026 I didn\u2019t know there was anything to check before
        that. I really thought I had just signed up for a normal promotion."
      unlockedFactIds:
      - sim_card_created
  - npcLine: I just want to make sure the SIM is cancelled and that nobody can use
      my identity for anything else.
    choices:
    - playerChoice: No worries, we will get in touch with the telco and ask them
        to shut that SIM card down. Be more vigilant next time!
      npcResponse: Thank you so much, sorry for the trouble!
      unlockedFactIds: []
  howTheScamWorks: Scammers impersonate a telecommunications company and offer victims
    a limited-time promotion, such as a chance to earn $100 for signing up for a
    SIM card. The scammers collect the victim's NRIC details and may ask for a confirmation
    code sent to the victim's phone. The information and code can then be used to
    register a SIM card under the victim's name without their genuine understanding
    or consent.
  warningSigns: "\u2022 Unexpected offers from telecommunications companies. \n\u2022
    Promises of easy money for signing up for a SIM card. \n\u2022 Limited-time offers
    designed to create urgency. \n\u2022 Requests for NRIC details. \n\u2022 Requests
    for confirmation codes or OTPs sent to your phone. \n\u2022 A SIM card being
    registered under your name without your knowledge."
  howToAvoid: Verify promotions directly through the telecommunications company's
    official website or customer service channels. Do not share your NRIC details
    or confirmation codes with unverified callers or companies. Never share an OTP
    or confirmation code with someone else.
  whatToDoIfVictim: Contact the telecommunications company immediately if you suspect
    that a SIM card has been registered under your name. Ask them to investigate
    and terminate any unauthorised line or account. Secure your other accounts if
    you shared a confirmation code, monitor for suspicious activity and report the
    scam to the relevant authorities.
  caseFileTextSegments: []
  caseFileDropdowns: []
